# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Temporal validity — reified OWL-Time intervals
# The usage span of a term or individual is a first-class time:ProperInterval,
# so it can carry its own facts (precision, source, named era, overlaps).
# Attach via uo:validInterval. May be applied to an individual (a single value's
# span) or — via OWL 2 punning — to a class (the span a whole vocabulary was in
# use). An open-ended span omits time:hasEnd.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# uo:validInterval a owl:ObjectProperty ;
#     rdfs:subPropertyOf time:hasTime ;
#     rdfs:label   "valid interval"@en ;
#     rdfs:comment "The time interval during which this entity or term was in use."@en ;
#     rdfs:range   time:ProperInterval .
